      "expected_impact": "If the per-element fp32 Vector work hypothesis holds, selu_-timing-3 and selu_-timing-7 should move from 81.6/83.2 us toward the reference's 56.8/59.1 us (element rate 205 -> ~290 Gelem/s), lifting those two speedups from 0.70/0.71 to near 1.0 and raising geo_mean by roughly +0.04 to +0.05 on top of 1.00156. selu_-timing-11 (fp32) and all nine launch-bound cases must stay within noise. If the per-program-overhead alternative is the real limit instead, these two workloads will barely move, which is itself the decisive result: it would redirect the next round to the tile/grid axis (halving or doubling _BLOCK_MAX only for the large path) rather than to arithmetic.",
